# Send nothing to the Docker build except code (see Dockerfile, Dockerfile.deid and docs/hosting.md).
# Allowlist only: no .rds, .csv, .csv.gz, caches or notebook outputs can enter the build context, so neither
# image can contain study data. Both runtime stages copy only app.py, data.py, templates/ and static/, plus
# the speech notebook source (shown as read-only code) and what their builder stage made: the demo's rendered notebook pages (on synthetic data), or the hosted site's
# JupyterLite (lite/ settings + build_jupyterlite.sh + notebooks/*.py, built with no data at all).
*
!app.py
!data.py
!templates/
!static/
!requirements-notebooks.txt
!scripts/generate_synthetic_data.py
!scripts/render_notebooks.py
!notebooks/*.py
!scripts/build_jupyterlite.sh
!lite/*.json
!lite/requirements-build.txt
